// -fdiagnostics-color=always (gcc's spelling; this test's .flags) colours a
// diagnostic on any stream — here the runner's pipe, which auto (the
// default) leaves plain (testdiagstartcol): the locus and message 1;37, the
// severity 1;31, the caret 1;32 (split arc Phase 0.5). The code above must
// stay on line 1.
//
// Oracle: gcc 13 -fdiagnostics-color=always on the same line as a .c file
// colours its piped stderr at 1:24 (its own palette: 01 the locus, 01;31
// `error:` and the `^~~` under foo); -fdiagnostics-color=auto on the pipe
// prints no SGR.
